 "explain": "'Probably' gives the unit probability 0.8 in the ordinary Stage-2 way, which the pipeline converts to evidence 0.6 before clausification; the fixture records the three layers separately (source probability, compiled evidence, backend-reported confidence). The actor is a robot so that no library default supplies a second proof: S3's stated-endpoint path is the sole support. Under encoding v2 the unit compiles to one executability path that holds the evidence itself, with no helper clause, and an uncertain rule counts once per action application: Q2 and the one-step plan Q3 report 0.6. The alternative_support variant is the original Ann text, kept as a control without a numeric pin.",
 "notes": "Amended 2026-09-11 (review R1): actor changed from Ann to Robo; probability and evidence layers separated; the per-clause 0.8 assertion and the 0.64 story removed. Astra review 5.3. Inspect _distribute_clause_confidence in solver/lc_packages.py before reuse. Amended 2026-09-20 (re-review RR3: strict_control Q2 backend []). Amended 2026-09-20 (WP06 review R3: variants probably_not_available and uninformative_location pin the p <= 0.5 boundary of physical_v1). Amended 2026-09-23 (encoding v2, gold review 0.4): Q1 (capability) is removed from the base, strict_control and alternative_support; the two unsupported-confidence variants ask the executable question Q2 with the same source-level diagnostic; Q2 and Q3 pin 0.6 directly and lose the shared_source_confidence requirement, because v2 has no helper and a one-step proof applies S3 once."
}
